@startuml
title P1 Telegram Route and Rollout States

hide empty description

state "Voice route" as Route {
  [*] --> processing
  processing --> pending : media ready + default committed
  processing --> failed : common ingest failure
  pending --> selected : callback replacement commits first
  pending --> dismissed : user keeps default
  pending --> started : default playback commits first
  pending --> expired : callback lifetime ends; default remains
  selected --> [*]
  dismissed --> [*]
  started --> [*]
  failed --> [*]
  expired --> [*]
}

state "Exposure" as Exposure {
  [*] --> withdrawn
  withdrawn --> coordinator_ready : additive schema + auth verified
  coordinator_ready --> clients_ready : exact capabilities registered
  clients_ready --> read_only : history / presence bounded cohort
  read_only --> mutations : DND / block / history actions
  mutations --> telegram_enabled : attachments / inline callbacks last
  telegram_enabled --> draining : rollback begins at owner surfaces
  draining --> withdrawn : canonical work reaches stable state
}

note bottom of Exposure
  Audio/document routes have no default and remain explicit-action-only.
  Rollback never rewrites receipt state or drops additive tables.
end note

@enduml
